Q: If statement not working as intended in powershell script A: <p>The problem is that <code>Remove-AppxPackage</code> returns <code>$null</code> when it runs, so the <code>if</code> condition is always falsy and always falls into <code>else</code> it prints &quot;Removal Failed&quot;</p>
<p>This should fix it</p>
<pre><code>foreach ($AppName in $AppsToRemove) {
    Write-Host &quot;Attempting to remove $AppName...&quot;

    try {
        $package = Get-AppxPackage -Name $AppName
        if ($package) {
            $package | Remove-AppxPackage -AllUsers -ErrorAction Stop

            # Remove provisioned package so it doesn't reinstall
            Get-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online |
                Where-Object { $_.DisplayName -like $AppName } |
                Remove-AppxProvisionedPackage -Online -ErrorAction Stop

            Write-Host &quot;Removal Successful&quot;
        } else {
            Write-Host &quot;$AppName not found, skipping.&quot;
        }
    }
    catch {
        Write-Host &quot;Removal Failed: $_&quot;
    }
}
</code></pre>
